   1: # Story rlv.6: Delete `dice-engine.js` and its dead sidecar wiring
   2: 
   3: Status: review
   4: 
   5: ## Story
   6: 
   7: As a developer maintaining TM Game,
   8: I want the already-unreachable `dice-engine.js` admin dice roller and its orphaned wiring removed,
   9: so that the codebase stops carrying dead code that could mislead a future reader into thinking the
  10: admin app still has its own dice roller, or that this cleanup is still blocked on something.
  11: 
  12: ## CRITICAL — this is NOT what the epic row originally said. Read this before Task 1.
  13: 
  14: The epic's own row for rlv.6 originally read "Delete `dice-engine.js`'s standalone dice math once
  15: ported (rlv.4)" — implying this was a migration-completion cleanup, blocked on rlv.4 finishing first.
  16: **That premise was wrong, investigated and corrected 2026-08-24 before this story was written.**
  17: `dice-engine.js` (`public/js/admin/dice-engine.js`) is **already fully unreachable dead code**,
  18: completely independent of anything rlv.4 did:
  19: 
  20: - `public/js/admin.js:37` imports `initDiceEngine` but **never calls it anywhere in the file**
  21:   (confirmed by grep — the import is the only occurrence of the name).
  22: - `public/js/admin.js:320`'s `switchDomain()` has `if (domain === 'engine') { /* Engine tab removed
  23:   — dice, feeding, session tracker were Engine-only tools */ }` — a no-op that can never fire, because
  24: - `public/admin.html` has **no sidebar button with `data-domain="engine"`** and **no `#d-engine`/
  25:   `#engine-content` element anywhere** (confirmed: `grep -in engine public/admin.html` returns zero
  26:   matches). The Engine domain's own nav entry was already physically removed from the HTML.
  27: - This was already flagged in a 2026-06-17 investigation note
  28:   (`specs/investigations/2026-06-17-session-handover-to-peter.md:80`): "**#846** delete dead
  29:   `initDiceEngine` / `dice-engine.js` (zero callers, confirmed)."
  30: - Its sibling Engine-domain tools, `feeding-engine.js` and `session-tracker.js`, were **already
  31:   deleted** under issue #836 (`public/js/admin.js:38-41`'s own comment;
  32:   `server/tests/issue-836-legacy-tracker-cache-removed.test.js:38-43` proves both files are gone).
  33:   `dice-engine.js` is the one file of that original trio still physically present, purely because
  34:   #836 didn't catch it too.
  35: 
  36: **This story is plain dead-code deletion, safe today, with zero dependency on rlv.4/rlv.5.** rlv.4
  37: did not "port dice-engine.js's dice math out" — it built a fresh, independent implementation in
  38: `app.js`/`char-pools.js`, never touching `dice-engine.js` itself. Nothing in rlv.4's diff or rlv.5's
  39: (superseded) investigation changes what's safe to delete here.
  40: 
