  47:    through the `#dice-engine`/`#feeding-engine` rules (lines 2570-2756, ending at the blank line
  48:    before `/* ── Player View link on character detail ── */`) — is deleted in full. The **separate**
  49:    `#session-tracker` block starting at line 2760 (`/* SESSION TRACKER (Engine domain) */`) is
  50:    **NOT** touched by this story — see "What this story is NOT" below.
  51: 4. `tests/admin.spec.js`'s `test.describe('Admin — Engine Domain', ...)` block (currently lines
  52:    338-366 — 5 tests asserting `#dice-engine`/`#feeding-engine` render, has a character selector, has
  53:    a roll button) is deleted, since the feature it tests no longer exists.
  54: 5. `tests/admin.spec.js`'s single `test('clicking Engine switches domain', ...)` (currently lines
  55:    156-159, inside `test.describe('Admin — Sidebar', ...)`) is deleted — it asserts on a
  56:    `data-domain="engine"` button and `#d-engine` element that no longer exist and never will again
  57:    once this story lands; the concept of "the Engine domain" is fully retired, not just its dice tool.
  58: 6. A new vitest suite (mirroring `server/tests/issue-836-legacy-tracker-cache-removed.test.js`'s own
  59:    pattern exactly — source-text/`fs.existsSync` checks, not a live import, since `admin.js`
  60:    transitively pulls in browser globals) proves: `public/js/admin/dice-engine.js` no longer exists;
  61:    `admin.js` no longer imports `initDiceEngine` or references `./admin/dice-engine.js`; `admin.js`'s
  62:    `switchDomain()` no longer has an `if (domain === 'engine')` branch; `admin-layout.css` no longer
  63:    contains a `#dice-engine` rule.
  64: 7. Every OTHER admin domain (Player, City, Spheres, Downtime, Attendance/Next-Session, Data,
  65:    Ordeals, Rules) continues to render and switch exactly as before — this is a pure subtraction of
  66:    already-dead code, not a restructuring of `switchDomain()`'s other branches or `admin-layout.css`'s
  67:    other rules.
